<section class="ui-card ui-prose"><h2>A place for each workflow</h2><dl><dt>Automatic protection</dt><dd>Choose datasets, retention, and timing under <a href="<?= zfsas_ui_url('snapshots', 'automation') ?>">Snapshots → Automation</a>. Dry Run previews actions without creating or deleting snapshots.</dd><dt>Individual snapshots</dt><dd>Browse a dataset, filter its snapshots, then review the exact selection before approving bulk actions. Used and Written measure different properties; neither guarantees reclaimable space.</dd><dt>Another copy</dt><dd>Configure source and destination jobs in <a href="<?= zfsas_ui_url('replication') ?>">Replication</a>. Transfers use their own checkpoint chain. Holds, incremental bases, and destination identities remain protected.</dd><dt>Understanding a wait</dt><dd>Open an operation in <a href="<?= zfsas_ui_url('activity') ?>">Activity</a> for its reported dependency, retry deadline, or resource constraint. A scheduled time is an occurrence, not a guarantee that execution can start immediately.</dd></dl></section>
<section class="ui-card ui-prose" id="recovery"><h2>Cancellation and recovery</h2><p>Cancel saves the decision before stopping workers. “Stopping” means shutdown is still being verified. Canceling a scheduled run pauses its schedule until you explicitly Resume.</p><p>Runtime queues, progress, and recent history live in RAM and disappear after reboot. Persistent pauses and essential migration recovery checkpoints survive. Interrupted manual sends require explicit Retry; Snapshot Manager batches require a fresh review, and previous per-item results may be unavailable.</p><p>This development build does not promise exactly-once execution across a reboot. Full replication coordination remains unfinished. Legacy pending finalizers without verified child identity evidence fail safely and require review.</p></section>
<section class="ui-card ui-prose"><h2>Schedules and saved settings</h2><p>New intervals start one interval after Save. Run Now and completion do not move that cadence. Existing schedules retain their actual timing until you explicitly convert them. Previews use the host timezone.</p><p>Saving configuration and applying it to the scheduler are separate results. If scheduler application fails, the saved configuration remains visible; follow the reported error. Run Now uses saved configuration, so save or discard pending edits first.</p></section>
<section class="ui-card"><h2>Report an issue</h2><p>Include a description of the problem, which system is affected, how to reproduce it, the plugin version, and the Unraid version. Attach a reviewed diagnostics zip when it helps explain runtime or queue problems.</p><div class="toolbar"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/adnanklink/zfssnapsync-unraid/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open GitHub issues</a><a class="btn" href="<?= zfsas_ui_url('tools') ?>">Get diagnostics</a></div></section>

